    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-10809",
      "problem": "For the function $y = f(x)$ shown below, what is the domain of the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14242843/assets/adf44ae3f3c8cb3bbe1958cca12e559b68d4d95247d087c69cb90425dbc05785.png)",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function $f^{-1}(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the range of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\n0 \\leq f(x) \\lt 9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n0 \\leq x \\lt 9.\n$$",
